WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:05.331
Hello, and welcome to week six: short division, exact answers.

2
00:00:05.331 --> 00:00:08.895
By the end, you will be able to divide using short division.

3
00:00:08.895 --> 00:00:10.749
Let's start.

4
00:00:11.899 --> 00:00:19.062
Make six hundred and eighty-four with counters: six hundreds, eight tens and four ones.

5
00:00:19.062 --> 00:00:23.950
Share them into two equal groups, hundreds first.

6
00:00:23.950 --> 00:00:27.249
Pause the video and have a go.

7
00:00:35.899 --> 00:00:39.812
Six hundreds divided by two equals three hundreds each,

8
00:00:39.812 --> 00:00:43.620
eight tens divided by two equals four tens each,

9
00:00:43.620 --> 00:00:48.391
four ones divided by two equals two ones each.

10
00:00:48.391 --> 00:00:51.526
Each group has three hundred and forty-two.

11
00:00:51.526 --> 00:00:56.375
In the bus stop, each digit of the answer sits above its column.

12
00:00:58.275 --> 00:01:03.697
Share the same six hundred and eighty-four into three groups instead.

13
00:01:03.697 --> 00:01:07.588
Pause the video and have a go.

14
00:01:16.238 --> 00:01:20.627
Six hundreds divided by three equals two hundreds each.

15
00:01:20.627 --> 00:01:26.861
Eight tens divided by three equals two tens each, and two tens are left.

16
00:01:26.861 --> 00:01:33.107
They cannot go into every group, so exchange them: two tens equals twenty ones.

17
00:01:33.107 --> 00:01:37.287
In the bus stop, write a small two before the four:

18
00:01:37.287 --> 00:01:43.912
now there are twenty-four ones, and twenty-four divided by three equals eight each.

19
00:01:45.812 --> 00:01:49.736
Now share six hundred and eighty-four into four groups.

20
00:01:49.736 --> 00:01:53.036
Pause the video and have a go.

21
00:02:01.686 --> 00:02:07.723
Six hundreds divided by four equals one hundred each, and two hundreds are left.

22
00:02:07.723 --> 00:02:11.996
Exchange them: two hundreds equals twenty tens.

23
00:02:11.996 --> 00:02:18.509
Write a small two before the eight: twenty plus eight equals twenty-eight tens,

24
00:02:18.509 --> 00:02:23.861
and twenty-eight tens divided by four equals seven tens each.

25
00:02:23.861 --> 00:02:28.803
Four ones divided by four equals one each.

26
00:02:30.703 --> 00:02:34.534
Share six hundred and eighteen into three groups.

27
00:02:34.534 --> 00:02:37.786
Pause the video and have a go.

28
00:02:46.436 --> 00:02:50.511
Six hundreds divided by three equals two hundreds each.

29
00:02:50.511 --> 00:02:55.666
One ten will not go into three groups, so each group gets zero tens:

30
00:02:55.666 --> 00:03:00.194
write the zero, so the six stays in the ones.

31
00:03:00.194 --> 00:03:04.362
Exchange the ten: ten plus eight equals eighteen ones,

32
00:03:04.362 --> 00:03:09.606
and eighteen divided by three equals six.

33
00:03:11.506 --> 00:03:14.234
Multiplying undoes dividing.

34
00:03:14.234 --> 00:03:18.704
Three groups of two hundred and six are six hundreds and eighteen ones;

35
00:03:18.704 --> 00:03:24.950
exchange ten ones for one ten, and that is six hundred and eighteen, the number we shared.

36
00:03:24.950 --> 00:03:29.568
So the answer is right, zero tens and all.

37
00:03:31.468 --> 00:03:33.825
Here is a worked example.

38
00:03:33.825 --> 00:03:40.752
Work out four hundred and ninety-two divided by four using short division.

39
00:03:42.002 --> 00:03:45.427
Four hundreds divided by four equals one;

40
00:03:45.427 --> 00:03:49.723
nine tens divided by four equals two remainder one:

41
00:03:49.723 --> 00:03:55.458
exchange one for ten ones; twelve ones divided by four equals three.

42
00:03:55.458 --> 00:03:56.956
Pause the video.

43
00:03:56.956 --> 00:03:59.813
Try the next one in your booklet.

44
00:04:09.113 --> 00:04:11.354
Now let's try a question together.

45
00:04:11.354 --> 00:04:16.880
Work out five hundred and sixty-eight divided by four using short division.

46
00:04:16.880 --> 00:04:20.284
Pause the video and have a go.

47
00:04:28.934 --> 00:04:35.645
Five hundreds divided by four equals one remainder one: exchange one for ten tens;

48
00:04:35.645 --> 00:04:43.029
sixteen tens divided by four equals four; eight ones divided by four equals two.

49
00:04:43.029 --> 00:04:45.602
Well done if you got it.

50
00:04:47.502 --> 00:04:49.360
Now try it in your booklet.

51
00:04:49.360 --> 00:04:54.085
Remember: share each column into the groups, biggest first;

52
00:04:54.085 --> 00:04:58.868
a counter that will not share is exchanged for ten of the next column,

53
00:04:58.868 --> 00:05:03.129
and a column with none for each group gets a zero.

54
00:05:03.129 --> 00:05:04.681
Good luck.
